[{"page":1,"text":"MINUTES OF A REGULAR\n\nCITY COUNCIL MEETING\n\nJanuary 27, 2026, at 6:10 PM\n\nPresent\n\nCouncilmember Parker McCumber\n\nCouncilmember Jacob Wood\n\nCouncilmember Jacob Holdaway\n\nCouncilmember David Lauret\n\nCouncilmember Ezra Nair\n\nAbsent\n\nMayor Zack Stratton\n\nStaff Present: City Manager Eric Ellis, Chief Deputy Holden Rockwell with the Utah County\nSheriff’s Office, Communications Director Jenna Ahern, Parks and Rec Director Brian Vawdrey,\nTreasurer Zack Adams, Interim City Attorney Jesse Riddle and Deputy City Recorder Tony Lara\nOthers Speaking: Vineyard residents Wayne Holdaway, Darlene Price, Sara Cameron, Chip Price,\n\nKaren Cornelius, and Tim Blackburn\n\n1.\n\nCALL TO ORDER/INVOCATION/INSPIRATIONAL THOUGHT/PLEDGE OF\n\nALLEGIANCE\n\nDeputy Recorder Tony Lara called the meeting to order at 6:10pm. He called for a\nmotion to nominate one of the councilmembers to serve as Mayor Pro Tempore.\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER MCCUMBER NOMINATED COUNCILMEMBER\n\nLAURET TO SERVE AS MAYOR PRO TEMPORE DURING MAYOR\n\nSTRATTON’S ABSENCE. COUNCILMEMBER HOLDAWAY SECONDED. THE\n\nROLL CALL WAS AS FOLLOWS: COUNCILMEMBERS MCCUMBER,\n\nHOLDAWAY, WOOD, LAURET, AND NAIR VOTED IN FAVOR. THE MOTION\n\nPASSED UNANIMOUSLY.\n\nMr. Lara turned time over to Mayor Pro Tempore Lauret to conduct the meeting.\nVineyard resident Wayne Holdaway offered a prayer and led the pledge of allegiance.\n\n2.\n\nPRESENTATIONS/RECOGNITIONS/AWARDS/PROCLAMATIONS\n\n2.1. Presentation on closed sessions\nAt the request of City Council, Deputy City Recorder Tony Lara will present on the\n\nPage 1 of 5; January 27, 2026, City Council Agenda","ocr":false},{"page":2,"text":"current policy of noticing closed sessions on each agenda.\nMr. Lara presented on the current practice of noticing closed sessions on each meeting\nagenda.\nThe council, along with staff, discussed changing that policy. It was decided that moving\nforward closed sessions would only appear on the agenda on an as needed basis.\n\n3.\n\nWORK SESSION\n\nThere were no work session items addressed in this meeting.\n\n4.\n\nPUBLIC COMMENTS\nDarlene Price, living in The Villas subdivision, asked that closed sessions in the future\nbe done either before or after the meeting to avoid having the public wait for the public\ncomment period.\nSara Cameron, living in the Parkside subdivision, addressed changes in policy and loss\nof staff.\nChip Price, living in the Providence subdivision, expressed support for the proposed\npolicy changes.\nKaren Cornelius, living in The Villas subdivision, thanked the council for the work on\nincreasing involvement from residents. She also wanted to remind the public about the\nimportance of addressing issues and not individuals during public comment.\nTim Blackburn, living in the Sleepy Ridge subdivision, asked the council to revisit the\nplan to place a cemetery in Vineyard. Additionally, he asked the council to look into the\nprocess of getting a post office within city limits.\n\nCouncilmember Holdaway commented on recent staff changes.\n\nMayor Pro Tempore Lauret responded to questions and statements made during public\nthe public comment period.\n\n5.\n\nMAYOR AND COUNCILMEMBERS' REPORTS/DISCLOSURES/RECUSALS\n\nCouncilmember McCumber’s report to the council.\n\nCouncilmember Holdaway’s report to the council.\n\nPage 2 of 5; January 27, 2026, City Council Agenda","ocr":false},{"page":3,"text":"Councilmember Nair’s report to the council.\n\nMayor Pro Tempore Lauret’s report to the council.\n\n6.\n\nSTAFF, COMMISSION, AND COMMITTEE REPORTS\n\nMayor Pro Tempore Lauret reported on the work that had been done so far with the staffing\nsubcommittee.\n\n7.\n\nCONSENT ITEMS\n\n7.1. Approval of the January 14, 2026, City Council Meeting Minutes\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER MCCUMBER MOVED TO APPROVE THE CONSENT ITEM\n\nAS PRESENTED. COUNCILMEMBER WOOD SECONDED. MAYOR PRO TEMPORE\n\nLAURET AND COUNCILMEMBERS NAIR, WOOD, HOLDAWAY AND MCCUMBER\n\nVOTED IN FAVOR. THE MOTION PASSED UNANIMOUSLY.\n\n8.\n\nAPPOINTMENTS/REMOVALS\n\n9.\n\nBUSINESS ITEMS\n\n9.1. Municipal Code Title 2 and 3 Amendments\n\nDISCUSSION AND ACTION: Interim City Attorney Jesse Riddle, with Deer Valley\nLaw, will present proposed changes to municipal codes title 2 and 3. The City Council\nwill act to approve (or Deny) these changes via Ordinance.\n\nInterim City Attorney Jesse Riddle presented the proposed changes and noted proposed\namendments to the ordinance during the presentation. There was discussion amongst council, in\nconjunction with some staff, regarding changes to employment status, appointments and\nremoval of appointed staff and other various changes that were in the proposed ordinance.\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER MCCUMBER MOVED TO ADOPT ORDINANCE 202601 AS AMENDED. THE MOTION WAS TABLED TO ENTERTAIN AN AMENDED\n\nMOTION PROPOSED BY COUNCILMEMBER NAIR.\n\nCounter Motion: COUNCILMEMBER NAIR MOVED TO CONTINUE THE ITEM TO\n\nTHE NEXT MEETING.\nThe council discussed the motions. It was decided that the council would vote on the motion\nbut revisit both title 2 and 3 at a future meeting to see if further revisions were necessary.\n\nMotion: MAYOR PRO TEMPORE LAURET BROUGHT BACK THE ORIGINAL\nPage 3 of 5; January 27, 2026, City Council Agenda","ocr":false},{"page":4,"text":"MOTION PRESENTED BY COUNCILMEMBER MCCUMBER. COUNCILMEMBER\n\nHOLDAWAY SECONDED. THE ROLL CALL WAS AS FOLLOWS: MAYOR PRO\n\nTEMPORE LAURET AND COUNCILMEMBERS NAIR, WOOD, HOLDAWAY AND\n\nMCCUMBER VOTED IN FAVOR. THE MOTION PASSED UNANIMOUSLY.\n\n9.2. ARCH Commission RAP Tax Grant Awards (Resolution 2026-06)\n\nJarom Sidwell, VIneyard's ARCH Commission Chair, will present ARCH's\nrecommendations to City Council for dispersing of the ARCH Grant.\n\nStaff recommended the council vote to continue this item so that the approval\ntime frame aligned with the time frame in the by-laws of the ARCH Commission.\n\nCouncilmember McCumber asked staff questions regarding the proposed grant\nawards. A short discussion ensued.\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER HOLDAWAY MOVED TO CONTINUE THE\n\nITEM TO A FUTURE MEETING. COUNCILMEMBER NAIR SECONDED.\n\nMAYOR PRO TEMPORE LAURET AND COUNCILMEMBERS NAIR, WOOD,\n\nHOLDAWAY AND MCCUMBER VOTED IN FAVOR. THE MOTION PASSED\n\nUNANIMOUSLY.\n\n9.3. PUBLIC HEARING - Adoption of the Fiscal Year 2025-2026 Working Budget\nafter Amendment #3 (Resolution 2026-05)\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER MCCUMBER MOVED TO ENTER INTO A PUBLIC\n\nHEARING AT 10:16PM. COUNCILMEMBER HOLDAWAY SECONDED. MAYOR PRO\n\nTEMPORE LAURET AND COUNCILMEMBERS NAIR, WOOD, HOLDAWAY AND\n\nMCCUMBER VOTED IN FAVOR. THE MOTION PASSED UNANIMOUSLY.\n\nCity Manager Eric Ellis reviewed the proposed changes in the budget amendment.\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER MCCUMBER MOVED TO CLOSE THE PUBLIC\n\nHEARING AT 10:25PM. COUNCILMEMBER WOOD SECONDED. MAYOR PRO\n\nTEMPORE LAURET AND COUNCILMEMBERS NAIR, WOOD, HOLDAWAY AND\n\nMCCUMBER VOTED IN FAVOR. THE MOTION PASSED UNANIMOUSLY.\n\nThe council discussed the proposed changes.\n\nMotion: COUNCILMEMBER HOLDAWAY MOVED TO ADOPT RESOLUTION\n\n2026-05 AMENDING THE FISCAL YEAR 2025-2026 BUDGET AS PRESENTED.\n\nCOUNCILMEMBER MCCUMBER SECONDED. THE ROLL CALL WAS AS\nPage 4 of 5; January 27, 2026, City Council Agenda","ocr":false},{"page":5,"text":"FOLLOWS: MAYOR PRO TEMPORE LAURET AND COUNCILMEMBERS\n\nMCCUMBER, HOLDAWAY AND WOOD VOTED IN FAVOR. COUNCILMEMBER\n\nNAIR VOTED NO. THE MOTION PASSED WITH A VOTE OF FOUR (4) TO ONE (1).\n\nCouncilmember McCumber asked the council for support in adding a working session to the\nnext meeting to discuss the budget process.\n\n10. CLOSED SESSION\n\nThere was no closed session during this meeting.\n\n11. ADJOURNMENT\n\nThe meeting was adjourned at 10:37pm\n\nMINUTES APPROVED ON:\n\n2/3/2026\n\nCERTIFIED CORRECT BY:\n\nTONY LARA, DEPUTY CITY RECORDER\n\nPage 5 of 5; January 27, 2026, City Council Agenda","ocr":false}]